<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Corbie Abbey</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Corbie Abbey was a Benedictine monastery in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picardy">Picardy</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, founded around 657 by Queen Balthild. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingians</a> it became a leading centre of learning and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> copying, where an early form of Caroline minuscule script was used. Its monks founded Corvey in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> in 822, and the abbey survived until the French Revolution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/corbie-abbey.jpg" alt="Corbie Abbey" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Markus3 (Marc ROUSSEL) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Corbie_abbatiale_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
